.TH wmwallpaper 1 "2025" "Window Maker"
.SH NAME
wmwallpaper \- choose the Window Maker desktop wallpaper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmwallpaper
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ folder ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmwallpaper
shows the images found in a folder (and up to three levels of its
subfolders) as a list of miniatures, with a preview of how the selected
image will look on the screen using the chosen placement (scaled, tiled,
centered, fit or fill).
.PP
When more than one monitor is present, the wallpaper can be applied either
to all monitors, setting \fBWorkspaceBack\fP, or only to the monitor under
the pointer, setting its entry in \fBMonitorSpecificBack\fP.
.PP
If no \fIfolder\fP is given, \fI~/GNUstep/Library/WindowMaker/Backgrounds\fP
is used, falling back to the system Window Maker or desktop wallpaper
folders when it is missing or empty.
The same chooser is available as the Wallpaper panel of \fBWPrefs\fP(1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " host:display.screen"
specify display to use.
.TP
.BR \-\-help " | " \-h
print a help message with the list of options and exit
.TP
.BR \-\-version " | " \-v
print the version of Window Maker from which the program comes and exit
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/GNUstep/Defaults/WindowMaker
Window Maker defaults, where the wallpaper settings are stored.
.TP
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/WindowMaker/wallpapers
cached miniatures (\fI~/.cache\fP is used if \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fP is not set).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR WPrefs (1),
.BR wmsetbg (1),
.BR wmaker (1)
